    24	/**
    25	 * The claims on a sheet: listed per person newest first, added, edited and moved through their
    26	 * statuses one at a time. Only a DRAFT can be edited. A voided claim keeps
    27	 * its number, which is never reused; a claim opened while period numbering is on is numbered within its
    28	 * period instead of sheet-wide. Settling a claim fixes its due at the rate its person's grade has then on the claim's date
    29	 * (at least the sheet's floor then), or at the
    30	 * figure a statement bound it to, plus the late charge it has then. No claim dated inside a closed period can be added, edited or moved,
    31	 * and no claim dated after its person's retirement date can be added or edited to that date. A clerk
    32	 * settling a claim whose due is above the sheet's clerk limit leaves it PENDING instead; a steward settles
    33	 * anything, and approves a PENDING claim (settling it, its due fixed then) or rejects it with a reason
    34	 * (back to OPEN); the user who opened a claim cannot approve it. A steward re-settles a SETTLED claim,
    35	 * fixing its due again at the figure it would have today as an OPEN claim bound by no statement. A claim
    36	 * with a negative amount is a correction: it is added or edited only when it names, by number, a SETTLED
    37	 * claim of the same person, and only a correction names one.
    38	 */
